{
  "$comment": "The shared `$now` conformance fixture (compat/model/README.md § Values). `$now` is the client's clock when a call is made, in epoch milliseconds, plus `offsetMillis`. Every suite's unit tests read this file with the clock pinned to `instant`. `valid` pins what each spelling evaluates to. `invalid` pins the spellings every reader of the IR's JSON refuses: the generator and the python-sdk, node-js-sdk and cli interpreters. `invalidArguments` pins what every runtime's `Now(unit, offsetMillis)` refuses, including the four typed runtimes, which are handed those two arguments by emitted source rather than the JSON. `call` pins one instant per call: its params are evaluated with a clock that moves on by `tickMillis` every time it is read, so a runtime that read the clock twice in one call would send something other than `sent`. A suite that cannot see this file here fails when OVERCAST_COMPAT_FIXTURES_REQUIRED is set, exactly as the error and blob fixtures do.",
